IS THE SCORE THREE CLUSTERS OR ONE SPREAD?
  real       n=189761  sd=2.499  skew=+0.929  excess kurtosis=+1.440
    KDE peaks by bandwidth: 0.15->1  0.20->1  0.25->1  0.30->1  0.40->1
    BIC k=1 886111   k=2 862292   k=3 861318   -> best k=3
  surrogate  n=189668  sd=2.637  skew=+1.253  excess kurtosis=+3.101
    KDE peaks by bandwidth: 0.15->1  0.20->1  0.25->1  0.30->1  0.40->1
    BIC k=1 906072   k=2 871519   k=3 870792   -> best k=3

  quantiles of the real score
    1%:-4.52  5%:-3.62  10%:-3.01  25%:-1.82  33%:-1.32  50%:-0.46  67%:+0.49  75%:+1.12  90%:+3.17  95%:+4.63  99%:+7.53
    the tercile cuts sit at -1.315 and +0.486, 0.72 sd apart

  READ THIS TOGETHER. Three well-separated clusters would show three KDE peaks at
  most bandwidths, a BIC minimum at k=3, and NEGATIVE excess kurtosis. One
  continuous spread shows a single peak, k=1 or k=2 on BIC, and kurtosis at or
  above zero.

