PART ONE -- IS THE CHOP SCORE CONCENTRATED?
  the five existing components: hold, tests, fails, inside, revert
  they are all present -- boundary tests, time inside, reversion
  crossings, failed breaks, pullback hold. chop |sep| = 0.122

  DROP-ONE on the existing five (holdout |sep|)
    without hold        0.073  (-0.049)
    without tests       0.155  (+0.033)
    without fails       0.114  (-0.008)
    without inside      0.121  (-0.001)
    without revert      0.115  (-0.007)

  correlation of each component with the chop score
    hold        r = +0.296
    tests       r = +0.632
    fails       r = +0.448
    inside      r = +0.749
    revert      r = +0.531

  THREE NEW COMPONENTS
  chop |sep| with all 8 components: 0.082  (-0.040 vs five)
    vr_short    alone 0.286 | dropping it 0.080 (-0.002) | r with old chop -0.082
    hold_ratio  alone 0.034 | dropping it 0.088 (+0.006) | r with old chop +0.699
    width_stab  alone 0.053 | dropping it 0.084 (+0.002) | r with old chop +0.009

  NULLS on the new components, 12 draws
    vr_short    real 0.286  surrogate 0.319  corrected -0.033
    hold_ratio  real 0.034  surrogate 0.079  corrected -0.045
    width_stab  real 0.053  surrogate 0.024  corrected +0.029
    chop (all)  real 0.082  surrogate 0.103  corrected -0.021

