score_q -- converting a convention into a decision
  CRITERION DECLARED BEFORE LOOKING: (a) separation, trend AND chop,
  (b) median run >= 20 bars, (c) every state >= 5% share.
  TIE RULE: the default 0.50 wins unless a challenger beats it on the
  SMALLER of its trend/chop separations by more than 1 paired
  block-bootstrap SE (21-bar blocks, 200 draws).
  Decided on IS 1999-2015. The holdout is read ONCE, at the end, for
  the chosen value only.

  aligned in-sample rows: 115165 (identical across all five candidates)
  q=0.40  sep trend 0.1777 chop 0.1419 (worst 0.1419) | run  20 | flip 0.0348 | min share 0.100
  q=0.45  sep trend 0.1728 chop 0.1394 (worst 0.1394) | run  19 | flip 0.0348 | min share 0.139
  q=0.50  sep trend 0.1735 chop 0.1334 (worst 0.1334) | run  19 | flip 0.0342 | min share 0.187
